    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0328" n="263" xml:id="pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.84/64: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-04">May 4, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>146. Your 246, May 4, midnight, to Murray. You should inform the Foreign Office
                    at once that this Government accepts with appreciation the offer to instruct the
                    British Legation at Addis Ababa to send a convoy to evacuate the entire American
                    Legation.</p>
                <p>Engert is being so informed.</p>
                <p>Please keep the Department fully and promptly informed of all further
                    developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
